; `:pred` is typed `.expr` — it requires a form whose head is an
; expression function, not a data form. Passing `(label)` (a data form)
; surfaces `wrong_underlying` at the slot path. Expression heads still
; flow cleanly into `.expr` slots (covered by core expression tests).
(plugin :name expr-result-test :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name cond
    (key :name pred :type expr :optional false))
  (form :name label))
